# DCC operating progress

Before adding fabricate, workshop checkout, Airtable, operator, or “pilot” features, read [`docs/dcc/OPERATING-PROGRESS.md`](docs/dcc/OPERATING-PROGRESS.md).

- That file is the Built / Partly / Not / Unknown scoreboard for the client + workshop loop.
- [`docs/dcc/STATUS.md`](docs/dcc/STATUS.md) is public-memory for routes and records — do not duplicate it.
- Do not mark a capability Built without a live route, record, payment, or demonstrated behavior.
- Do not invent paid jobs, operator commitments, entity/money decisions, or enable Stripe until OPERATING-PROGRESS says a DCC SKU and entity exist.
- After a real ship: update the checklist letter, add evidence, append a dated Progress log row.
